    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* --- The bracket, and the structure constants of so(3) --- */\nbr(X, Y) := ratsimp( X.Y - Y.X )$\n\n/* generators of rotation about the three axes (1.03) */\nLb : [ matrix([0,0,0],[0,0,-1],[0,1,0]),\n       matrix([0,0,1],[0,0,0],[-1,0,0]),\n       matrix([0,-1,0],[1,0,0],[0,0,0]) ]$\n\n/* Levi-Civita symbol for a permutation of (1,2,3) */\neps(i,j,k) := (j-i)*(k-i)*(k-j)/2$\n\nprint(\"so(3):  [Lᵢ, Lⱼ] compared with ε_ijk Lₖ\")$\nfor i:1 thru 3 do for j:1 thru 3 do\n  if i < j then block([B, k],\n    k : 6 - i - j,                       /* the remaining index */\n    B : br(Lb[i], Lb[j]),\n    print(\"   [L\", i, \", L\", j, \"] = \", B),\n    print(\"      ε_\", i, j, k, \" = \", eps(i,j,k),\n          \" ;  [Lᵢ,Lⱼ] − ε_ijk Lₖ = \", ratsimp( B - eps(i,j,k)*Lb[k] )) )$\nprint(\"   Zero in every case: the structure constants of so(3) are exactly\")$\nprint(\"   the Levi-Civita symbol.  (The (1,3) bracket gives −L₂, not +L₂ —\")$\nprint(\"   ε₁₃₂ = −1, since (1,3,2) is an odd permutation.)\")$\n\n/* --- so(3) ≅ (ℝ³, ×) --- */\nskew3(v) := v[1]*Lb[1] + v[2]*Lb[2] + v[3]*Lb[3]$\nvv : [v1, v2, v3]$  ww : [w1, w2, w3]$\ncross3(a, b) := [ a[2]*b[3] - a[3]*b[2],\n                  a[3]*b[1] - a[1]*b[3],\n                  a[1]*b[2] - a[2]*b[1] ]$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"the hat map v ↦ v̂ sending ℝ³ to so(3):\")$\nprint(\"   [v̂, ŵ] − (v×w)^ = \", ratsimp( br(skew3(vv), skew3(ww))\n                                        - skew3(cross3(vv,ww)) ))$\nprint(\"   so the cross product IS the Lie bracket of so(3).  The vector\")$\nprint(\"   algebra of 1.01 was a Lie algebra all along.\")$\nprint(\"   v̂ w − v × w = \", ratsimp( skew3(vv).transpose(matrix(ww))\n                                   - transpose(matrix(cross3(vv,ww))) ))$\n\n/* --- closure and Jacobi, on generic elements --- */\nXg : skew3([x1,x2,x3])$  Yg : skew3([y1,y2,y3])$  Zg : skew3([z1,z2,z3])$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"closure:   [X,Y] + [X,Y]ᵀ = \",\n      ratsimp( br(Xg,Yg) + transpose(br(Xg,Yg)) ),\n      \"  (still skew ✓)\")$\nprint(\"antisymmetry: [X,Y] + [Y,X] = \", ratsimp( br(Xg,Yg) + br(Yg,Xg) ))$\nprint(\"Jacobi:\")$\nprint(\"   [X,[Y,Z]] + [Y,[Z,X]] + [Z,[X,Y]] = \",\n      ratsimp( br(Xg,br(Yg,Zg)) + br(Yg,br(Zg,Xg)) + br(Zg,br(Xg,Yg)) ))$\nprint(\"   (which for the cross product is the Jacobi identity\")$\nprint(\"    a×(b×c) + b×(c×a) + c×(a×b) = 0 — the same statement.)\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 3,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "so(3):  [Lᵢ, Lⱼ] compared with ε_ijk Lₖ\n   [L 1 , L 2 ] =  matrix([0,-1,0],[1,0,0],[0,0,0])\n      ε_ 1 2 3  =  1  ;  [Lᵢ,Lⱼ] − ε_ijk Lₖ =  matrix([0,0,0],[0,0,0],[0,0,0])\n   [L 1 , L 3 ] =  matrix([0,0,-1],[0,0,0],[1,0,0])\n      ε_ 1 3 2  =  -1  ;  [Lᵢ,Lⱼ] − ε_ijk Lₖ =\n        matrix([0,0,0],[0,0,0],[0,0,0])\n   [L 2 , L 3 ] =  matrix([0,0,0],[0,0,-1],[0,1,0])\n      ε_ 2 3 1  =  1  ;  [Lᵢ,Lⱼ] − ε_ijk Lₖ =  matrix([0,0,0],[0,0,0],[0,0,0])\n   Zero in every case: the structure constants of so(3) are exactly\n   the Levi-Civita symbol.  (The (1,3) bracket gives −L₂, not +L₂ —\n   ε₁₃₂ = −1, since (1,3,2) is an odd permutation.)\nthe hat map v ↦ v̂ sending ℝ³ to so(3):\n   [v̂, ŵ] − (v×w)^ =  matrix([0,0,0],[0,0,0],[0,0,0])\n   so the cross product IS the Lie bracket of so(3).  The vector\n   algebra of 1.01 was a Lie algebra all along.\n   v̂ w − v × w =  matrix([0],[0],[0])\nclosure:   [X,Y] + [X,Y]ᵀ =  matrix([0,0,0],[0,0,0],[0,0,0])   (still skew ✓)\nantisymmetry: [X,Y] + [Y,X] =  matrix([0,0,0],[0,0,0],[0,0,0])\nJacobi:\n   [X,[Y,Z]] + [Y,[Z,X]] + [Z,[X,Y]] =  matrix([0,0,0],[0,0,0],[0,0,0])\n   (which for the cross product is the Jacobi identity\n    a×(b×c) + b×(c×a) + c×(a×b) = 0 — the same statement.)"
