    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "/* --- sl(2,ℝ), and the Killing fields of 4.07 --- */\ndeclare([x, y], real)$\nme : matrix([0,1],[0,0])$      /* e */\nmf : matrix([0,0],[1,0])$      /* f */\nmh : matrix([1,0],[0,-1])$     /* h */\n\nprint(\"sl(2,ℝ) in the standard basis:\")$\nprint(\"   [h,e] − 2e = \", br(mh,me) - 2*me)$\nprint(\"   [h,f] + 2f = \", br(mh,mf) + 2*mf)$\nprint(\"   [e,f] − h  = \", br(me,mf) - mh)$\n\n/* The vector field on the upper half-plane induced by M ∈ sl(2,ℝ) acting\n   by Möbius transformations z ↦ (az+b)/(cz+d).  Differentiating at t = 0\n   gives the complex field F(z) = b + (a−d)z − c z². */\nind(M) := block([F],\n  F : M[1][2] + (M[1][1]-M[2][2])*(x+%i*y) - M[2][1]*(x+%i*y)^2,\n  [ ratsimp(realpart(F)), ratsimp(imagpart(F)) ])$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"induced vector fields on the upper half-plane:\")$\nprint(\"   e ↦ \", ind(me), \"        (4.07's ∂x)\")$\nprint(\"   h ↦ \", ind(mh), \"        (4.07's x∂x + y∂y, doubled)\")$\nprint(\"   f ↦ \", ind(mf), \"   (4.07's (x²−y²)∂x + 2xy∂y, negated)\")$\n\n/* they are Killing for the hyperbolic metric — 4.07 again */\nlie_g(g, vars, X) := genmatrix( lambda([i,j], ratsimp(\n      sum( X[k]*diff(g[i][j], vars[k]), k,1,2)\n    + sum( g[k][j]*diff(X[k], vars[i]), k,1,2)\n    + sum( g[i][k]*diff(X[k], vars[j]), k,1,2) )), 2, 2)$\ngH : matrix([1/y^2,0],[0,1/y^2])$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"   each is Killing for g = (dx²+dy²)/y² :\")$\nfor M in [me, mh, mf] do print(\"      L_X g = \", lie_g(gH, [x,y], ind(M)))$\n\n/* --- the bracket of vector fields --- */\nvfbr(X, Y, vars) := makelist( ratsimp(\n  sum( X[i]*diff(Y[k], vars[i]) - Y[i]*diff(X[k], vars[i]), i, 1, 2) ),\n  k, 1, 2)$\n\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"Does ind() respect the bracket?\")$\nfor p in [[mh,me], [mh,mf], [me,mf]] do block([A, B, lhs, rhs],\n  A : p[1], B : p[2],\n  lhs : ind( br(A,B) ),\n  rhs : vfbr( ind(A), ind(B), [x,y] ),\n  print(\"   ind([A,B]) = \", lhs),\n  print(\"   [ind A, ind B] = \", rhs),\n  print(\"   lhs + rhs = \", ratsimp(lhs + rhs)) )$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"The two differ by a SIGN: ind([A,B]) = −[ind A, ind B], in all three\")$\nprint(\"cases.  This is not an error.  Sending X to the field that generates\")$\nprint(\"the flow of exp(tX) under a LEFT action is a Lie algebra ANTI-\")$\nprint(\"homomorphism for the usual vector-field bracket; the homomorphism\")$\nprint(\"convention uses exp(−tX), or the right action, and texts differ on\")$\nprint(\"which they adopt.  Either way the image is a 3-dimensional Lie\")$\nprint(\"algebra isomorphic to sl(2,ℝ) — the Lie algebra of PSL₂(ℝ), and the\")$\nprint(\"Killing algebra of the hyperbolic plane.\")$\nprint(\"\")$\nprint(\"So Stage 2's three groups reappear as three Lie algebras:\")$\nprint(\"   E(2)      →  so(2) ⋉ ℝ²   (not simple: translations are an ideal)\")$\nprint(\"   SO(3)     →  so(3) ≅ su(2)   compact, K > 0\")$\nprint(\"   PSL₂(ℝ)   →  sl(2,ℝ)         non-compact, K < 0\")$\nprint(\"Compactness of the group tracks the sign of the curvature.\")$",
      "metadata": {},
      "execution_count": 8,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "name": "stdout",
          "output_type": "stream",
          "text": [
            "sl(2,ℝ) in the standard basis:\n   [h,e] − 2e =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   [h,f] + 2f =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n   [e,f] − h  =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\ninduced vector fields on the upper half-plane:\n   e ↦  [1,0]         (4.07's ∂x)\n   h ↦  [2*x,2*y]         (4.07's x∂x + y∂y, doubled)\n   f ↦  [y^2-x^2,-(2*x*y)]    (4.07's (x²−y²)∂x + 2xy∂y, negated)\n   each is Killing for g = (dx²+dy²)/y² :\n      L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n      L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\n      L_X g =  matrix([0,0],[0,0])\nDoes ind() respect the bracket?\n   ind([A,B]) =  [2,0]\n   [ind A, ind B] =  [-2,0]\n   lhs + rhs =  [0,0]\n   ind([A,B]) =  [2*x^2-2*y^2,4*x*y]\n   [ind A, ind B] =  [2*y^2-2*x^2,-(4*x*y)]\n   lhs + rhs =  [0,0]\n   ind([A,B]) =  [2*x,2*y]\n   [ind A, ind B] =  [-(2*x),-(2*y)]\n   lhs + rhs =  [0,0]\nThe two differ by a SIGN: ind([A,B]) = −[ind A, ind B], in all three\ncases.  This is not an error.  Sending X to the field that generates\nthe flow of exp(tX) under a LEFT action is a Lie algebra ANTI-\nhomomorphism for the usual vector-field bracket; the homomorphism\nconvention uses exp(−tX), or the right action, and texts differ on\nwhich they adopt.  Either way the image is a 3-dimensional Lie\nalgebra isomorphic to sl(2,ℝ) — the Lie algebra of PSL₂(ℝ), and the\nKilling algebra of the hyperbolic plane.\nSo Stage 2's three groups reappear as three Lie algebras:\n   E(2)      →  so(2) ⋉ ℝ²   (not simple: translations are an ideal)\n   SO(3)     →  so(3) ≅ su(2)   compact, K > 0\n   PSL₂(ℝ)   →  sl(2,ℝ)         non-compact, K < 0\nCompactness of the group tracks the sign of the curvature."
          ]
